cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Pattern-Driven LLM Code Optimization Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for evaluating whether large language models can recognize
  and fix C-code inefficiency patterns that production compilers cannot
  optimize automatically. Includes 27 base patterns across 7 categories,
  a variant generator producing 1,140 dataset entries (700 composed
  multi-pattern variants spanning 23 distinct two- and three-pattern
  combinations), a 36-pattern post-cutoff held-out test set for
  contamination defense, a two-axis faithfulness verifier (differential
  equivalence + AST structural checks), setup-randomization and bootstrap
  CI protocols following Mytkowicz et al. (ASPLOS 2009), and a LoRA
  fine-tuning workflow with explicit held-out exclusion for transfer
  measurement.
type: software
